    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical checklist for testing local LLMs offline. The scenario assumes models can be downloaded beforehand and then the system disconnected. The core of this hypothetical test involves two key checks: first, verifying the model can generate coherent text outputs without any network access, ensuring all necessary components are locally available. Second, it mandates a thorough check for any network requests originating from the LLM or its inference engine during the offline period. It's crucial to reiterate that this is a theoretical framework; no actual offline tests have been performed within this context. The objective is to establish a clear, albeit unexecuted, procedure for validating offline LLM functionality and security. We aim to identify potential challenges and best practices for such a setup. Feedback on this proposed, hypothetical testing methodology is welcome.",
