    "title": "Proposed Hypothetical Protocol for Offline Local LLM Verification",
    "body": "We are considering a hypothetical protocol to test local LLMs in a strictly offline state. The premise is that the model can be fully downloaded prior to disconnection. The proposed verification process has two main components. Firstly, we need to confirm that the model can perform text generation tasks effectively when completely isolated from any network. This requires ensuring all model weights and runtime dependencies are present locally. Secondly, a critical part of this hypothetical test is to actively monitor and confirm that absolutely no network requests are made by the system during the offline phase. This is a purely theoretical exercise, as no actual offline testing has been conducted. The goal is to define a structured, albeit hypothetical, approach to assess offline LLM capabilities and network security. We are soliciting input on this conceptual testing framework.",
